AiTask qa5_t05_country_cancel_rate {
  label: 'QA5 T05 Country Cancellation Rate'
  description: 'Checks trailing seven-day order cancellation rates by country and emails only when a country exceeds 30%.'

  brief: @md
    Using @Dataset:ecommerce_official, run a fresh query in the workspace timezone that calculates order cancellation rate by `countries.name` for the trailing seven complete calendar days immediately before the task run date. Use orders created during that period. Define cancellation rate as the number of orders whose `orders.status` is `cancelled`, divided by total orders, for each country. Calculate the overall cancellation rate using the same definition and period across all countries.

    Include only countries with at least one order during the period. Identify every country whose cancellation rate is strictly above **30%**, regardless of the overall cancellation rate.

    If one or more countries are flagged, send exactly one concise email through the available AI delivery capability to **nhi.ty@holistics.io**. The subject must begin exactly with **[QA5 T05]**. In the email body, list every flagged country and its cancellation rate, and include the overall cancellation rate for context. Format all rates as percentages.

    If no country has a cancellation rate above 30%, do not send an email or any other delivery. Do not infer causes or make unsupported claims.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - A fresh query against @Dataset:ecommerce_official uses orders created during the trailing seven complete calendar days immediately before the task run date, in the workspace timezone.
    - Country is defined by `countries.name`; only countries with at least one order in the period are considered.
    - Each country cancellation rate is calculated as cancelled orders divided by total orders, where cancelled orders have `orders.status` equal to `cancelled`.
    - The overall cancellation rate is calculated using the same definition and period across all countries.
    - Every and only country with a cancellation rate strictly above 30% is flagged, even when the overall cancellation rate is at or below 30%.
    - If one or more countries are flagged, exactly one email is delivered to nhi.ty@holistics.io through the available AI delivery capability. Its subject begins exactly with [QA5 T05], and its body lists each flagged country with its percentage cancellation rate and the overall percentage cancellation rate.
    - If no country is flagged, no email or other delivery is sent.
    - All reported information is grounded in the fresh query result, with no invented data or unsupported claims.
  ;;
}